cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or research artifact, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Claimshift: A Manifest Protocol for Verification Inheritance"
authors:
  - family-names: Flyxion
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
repository-code: "https://github.com/8b-is/claimshift"
url: "https://github.com/8b-is/claimshift"
abstract: >
  Claimshift is a formal verification inheritance framework for scholarly
  artifacts under transformation. It addresses the fundamental question: when
  a verified claim is transformed, can the original verification be inherited
  by the successor? The project implements a three-paper series demonstrating
  that verification inheritance is undecidable in general but decidable within
  bounded rewrite fragments, and provides a manifest protocol for representing
  verification across transformations with proper role separation (assertion,
  verification, transformation attestation).
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - verification inheritance
  - mutation testing
  - Lean theorem prover
  - scholarly provenance
  - transformation attestation
  - claim graphs
  - proof assistant
